    cautions: "Two hazards: (1) biotoxins — Pismo clams are periodically closed by CDPH domoic-acid quarantines; and (2) legality/conservation — strict minimum size, a low daily limit, a mandatory measuring gauge, and slow-recovering, otter-predated populations. Undersized clams must be reburied where dug.",
