      texture: "Very smooth and glossy (varnished-looking), with fine concentric growth lines but no coarse ribs.",
      size: "Large and heavy — commonly 10-13 cm and up to ~18 cm (about 7 in) across in old animals.",
      shell: "Thick, dense, glossy triangular shell with a strong hinge; far heavier than most surf clams of similar size.",
      keyFeatures: ["Heavy, thick, glossy triangular-oval shell", "Smooth polished tan/buff surface with brownish radial bands", "No coarse radial ribs", "Buried in clean sand of open surf beaches (central/southern CA)"],
